{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AEFbPJLxj1aQqEVMuUNBpq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '核心叙事：novelty 被彻底否定（\"applying textbook MH 1988 to new data ≠ contribution\"），IRT\n2\t  misspecification 被视为 根本性方法论缺陷（\"98% |Lz|>2 → ability matching 系统性偏差 → 31% C% 是 artifact\n3\t  而非 finding\"）， semi-synthetic framework 被认为 too simple to publish，meta-critique 被\n4\t  dismiss 为 obvious。 每个实验的结果要么被重新解读为 artifact，要么被认为 underpowered/scope-limited。 reviewer\n5\t  立场：3 位中 2-3 位给 reject，平均分 3.5，novelty sub-score 1.5。 三条 reframe 路径（Framework-first\n6\t  / MIRT upgrade / Benchmark science）是唯一出路。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n11\t  plan_id: plan_001\n12\t  description: METABENCH MMLU 5,227×12,508 response matrix 上的 MH-DIF 分析\n13\t  expected_results:\n14\t    temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n15\t    temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.318\n16\t    temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n17\t    ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n18\t    within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n19\t    domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n20\t    domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n21\t    sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n22\t    irt_lz_pct_above_2: 98\n23\t    reviewer_interpretation: artifact_of_misspecification\n24\t  result_rationale: '数据本身与已完成 registry 一致——31.3% C% 是真实观测。但在 worst 档下，reviewer 的解读路径是：\n25\t    (1) 98% 模型 |Lz|>2 表明 1D IRT ability estimates 系统性不可靠； (2) MH 的 ability matching\n26\t    依赖 total score 作为 ability proxy，而 MMLU 57 subjects 的 multidimensionality 意味着 total\n27\t    score 是一个 collapsed composite，无法真正 match ability； (3) 因此 31.3% C% 中有大量是 ability\n28\t    confounding 造成的 spurious DIF—— 两个模型在不同 subject domains 上能力结构不同，但 total score 相近，被\n29\t    MH 视为 \"matched\"， 实际上它们在特定 subject 上的 ability 并不 matched； (4) enrichment≈0.96 直接验证了\n30\t    DIF flags 与已知 contamination labels 无关联—— reviewer 读为 \"你的方法检测不到 contamination\"；\n31\t    (5) 0.18% sanity check 虽然证明不是纯噪声，但 reviewer 认为这只是证明 temporal cohort 之间 确实存在 ability\n32\t    distribution shift，而非 item-level contamination。 ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 被 reviewer 解读为\n33\t    \"domain improvement 是 confound 的证据， 不是被排除的证据\"——因为 item-level decomposition (plan_019)\n34\t    的 pseudo R²=0.0007 只说明 linear relationship 弱，不排除 nonlinear 或 interaction effects。\n35\t\n36\t    '\n37\t  tables:\n38\t  - 'Table 1: Temporal DIF results — C%=31.3%, enrichment=0.96 — reviewer 标注 ''enrichment≈1\n39\t    = no detection value'''\n40\t  - 'Table 2: Cohort comparison — ability split C%=2.9% vs temporal 31.3% — reviewer\n41\t    认为差异来自 ability shift 而非 item-level effect'\n42\t  figures_description:\n43\t  - 'Fig 1: DIF effect size distribution — reviewer 指出 continuous distribution without\n44\t    bimodality suggests no distinct ''contaminated'' subpopulation, consistent with\n45\t    model misfit gradual shift'\n46\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 的核心攻击：31.3% 是一个 misspecified model 下的 baseline rate，不是 finding。\n47\t    类比：如果你用线性回归拟合非线性数据，residual patterns 不代表新发现，而代表 model misfit。 MH-DIF on multidimensional\n48\t    data with 1D matching = structural Type I error inflation。 Llama-2 vs Llama-3\n49\t    within-family C%=61.3% 被读为更强的证据——\"同一 family 内 61% items show DIF = 显然是 ability\n50\t    structure change, not contamination\"。\n51\t\n52\t    '\n53\t- name: rl_robustness_validation\n54\t  plan_id: plan_002\n55\t  description: 验证 DIF 对 reasoning-RL 模型（GRPO/PPO）的鲁棒性\n56\t  expected_results:\n57\t    n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n58\t    alignment_rl_cohort_n: 477\n59\t    grpo_cohort_dif_c_pct: 34.8\n60\t    sft_baseline_dif_c_pct: 30.2\n61\t    alignment_rl_dif_c_pct: 31.9\n62\t    jaccard_sft_vs_grpo: 0.71\n63\t    delong_p_dif_vs_constat: 0.38\n64\t    tost_equivalence_p: 0.22\n65\t    constat_auroc_on_rl: 0.54\n66\t    mink_auroc_on_rl: 0.51\n67\t    dif_auroc_on_rl: 0.58\n68\t    bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif:\n69\t    - 0.41\n70\t    - 0.73\n71\t    power_at_p04: 0.12\n72\t    power_at_p07: 0.43\n73\t    power_at_p10: 0.68\n74\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下的问题不是实验跑不出来，而是 N=13 reasoning-RL 模型被 reviewer 视为 fundamentally\n75\t    underpowered： (1) 13 个 GRPO/PPO 模型混入 focal cohort 后，C% 从 30.2% 微升到 34.8%—— reviewer\n76\t    解读为 \"adding stronger models → more ability confounding → more spurious DIF\"， 而非\n77\t    \"DIF robust to RL\"； (2) AUROC 比较（DIF 0.58 vs ConStat 0.54 vs Min-K% 0.51）差异不显著（DeLong\n78\t    p=0.38）， bootstrap CI 跨越 0.5——reviewer 说 \"all methods are at chance, you''ve shown\n79\t    nothing\"； (3) TOST equivalence test p=0.22，无法 reject \"DIF 和传统方法等效\" 的 H0—— reviewer\n80\t    认为 \"failure to demonstrate equivalence or superiority = uninformative\"； (4) Power\n81\t    analysis 显示 p=0.4 时 TPR=0.12——reviewer 说 \"DIF can only detect near-complete exploitation,\n82\t    which is the trivial case\"； (5) 核心问题：整个实验无法区分 \"DIF works on RL models\" 和 \"DIF\n83\t    produces same artifacts regardless of model type\"——在 IRT misspecification 框架下，两者不可区分。\n84\t\n85\t    '\n86\t  tables:\n87\t  - 'Table: AUROC comparison across 3 methods × 3 cohort types — all CIs overlap,\n88\t    no method dominates'\n89\t  - 'Table: Power curve p ∈ [0.4, 1.0] — reviewer notes ''useful range starts at p≥0.7,\n90\t    narrowing practical applicability'''\n91\t  figures_description:\n92\t  - 'Fig: Bootstrap AUROC distributions — heavy overlap among DIF/ConStat/Min-K%,\n93\t    all centered near 0.55'\n94\t  analysis: 'Reviewer consensus: \"N=13 RL models is a pilot, not a validation. The\n95\t    authors cannot claim RL-robustness based on mixing 13 models into a 600+ cohort\n96\t    — the signal is drowned. Individual-model analysis (ConStat/Min-K%) at least tests\n97\t    each model; DIF by design cannot. This is a structural limitation of group-level\n98\t    methods, acknowledged but not resolved.\" 致命打击：reviewer 将此解读为 DIF 的固有缺陷——无法做 per-model\n99\t    detection——而非优势。\n100\t\n101\t    '\n102\t- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n103\t  plan_id: plan_003a\n104\t  description: ConStat-style perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的独立评估\n105\t  expected_results:\n106\t    n_items_reformulated: 220\n107\t    reformulation_quality_human_eval: 0.82\n108\t    constat_detection_rate_non_rl: 0.41\n109\t    constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.08\n110\t    constat_fdr_controlled_rate: 0.23\n111\t    constat_vs_dif_overlap_pct: 12.7\n112\t    constat_fpr: 0.067\n113\t    constat_unique_detections: 158\n114\t    dif_unique_detections: 892\n115\t  result_rationale: 'ConStat 在 non-RL 模型上表现合理（41% detection rate），FPR 远低于 DIF（0.067\n116\t    vs 0.318）。 Worst 档下 reviewer 解读： (1) ConStat FPR=0.067 vs DIF FPR=0.318——\"DIF\n117\t    的高 detection rate 主要来自高 FPR， 不是真正的 detection power\"； (2) 12.7% overlap 表明两种方法检测的是完全不同的现象——reviewer\n118\t    认为 ConStat 检测 actual contamination (perturbation sensitivity)，而 DIF 检测 ability\n119\t    shift artifact； (3) ConStat 在 RL 模型上确实退化（8%），但 reviewer 说 \"at least ConStat has\n120\t    a clear mechanism story; DIF''s mechanism is unfalsifiable because any result\n121\t    can be attributed to either contamination or ability change\"； (4) 220 items 的\n122\t    reformulation 质量（0.82 human eval）足够，但 scope 太小—— reviewer 要求 full-scale replication\n123\t    才能比较。\n124\t\n125\t    '\n126\t  tables:\n127\t  - 'Table: ConStat vs DIF detection comparison — ConStat lower recall but much lower\n128\t    FPR'\n129\t  figures_description:\n130\t  - 'Fig: Venn diagram of ConStat vs DIF detections — minimal overlap underscores\n131\t    different phenomena detected'\n132\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 用 ConStat 的低 FPR 作为武器：\"ConStat achieves controlled FPR by design\n133\t    (FDR correction); DIF''s 31.8% FPR on Li-clean items means nearly 1 in 3 flags\n134\t    is false, and you cannot tell which ones without ground truth.\" 这强化了 \"DIF C% is\n135\t    inflated by misspecification\" 的叙事。\n136\t\n137\t    '\n138\t- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n139\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n140\t  description: DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的独立评估\n141\t  expected_results:\n142\t    n_models_evaluated: 12\n143\t    n_items_per_model: 200\n144\t    n_generations_per_item: 50\n145\t    bimodal_detection_rate: 0.14\n146\t    variance_based_detection_rate: 0.22\n147\t    dvd_vs_dif_overlap: 0.09\n148\t    dvd_fpr: 0.04\n149\t    gpu_hours_used: 65\n150\t    variant_contamination_detected: 31\n151\t  result_rationale: 'DVD 需要 per-model inference access（50 generations × 200 items\n152\t    × 12 models = 120K generations）， cost 高但可行。Worst 档下： (1) Bimodal detection rate\n153\t    仅 14%——reviewer 说 \"variant contamination is rare or this method is underpowered,\n154\t    either way not compelling\"； (2) 9% overlap with DIF——再次证明方法检测不同现象，但 worst 档下 reviewer\n155\t    解读为 \"three orthogonal weak signals don''t add up to one strong signal\"； (3) DVD\n156\t    FPR=0.04 很低，但 detection rate 也低——reviewer 认为 precision-recall tradeoff 不足以支撑 contribution；\n157\t    (4) 12 models 太少——reviewer 要求 \"at minimum 50+ models to characterize generation\n158\t    variance distribution\"，而 GPU budget 不支持。\n159\t\n160\t    '\n161\t  tables:\n162\t  - 'Table: DVD detection rates by contamination type (verbatim vs variant) — low\n163\t    overall'\n164\t  figures_description:\n165\t  - 'Fig: Generation variance histograms per model — most items unimodal, bimodal\n166\t    signal weak'\n167\t  analysis: 'DVD 作为独立信号太弱（14% bimodal detection），且 per-model inference 的 cost 使其不\n168\t    scalable。 Reviewer 建议 \"DVD is better suited as a follow-up diagnostic on flagged\n169\t    items, not a primary detector\" ——削弱 ensemble 的 motivation。\n170\t\n171\t    '\n172\t- name: ensemble_fusion\n173\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n174\t  description: DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合\n175\t  expected_results:\n176\t    majority_vote_precision: 0.38\n177\t    majority_vote_recall: 0.09\n178\t    weighted_fusion_precision: 0.44\n179\t    weighted_fusion_recall: 0.15\n180\t    ensemble_fpr: 0.087\n181\t    cross_val_weight_stability: low — std/mean > 0.6 across folds\n182\t    dif_weight: 0.28\n183\t    constat_weight: 0.51\n184\t    dvd_weight: 0.21\n185\t    uniform_baseline_vs_optimized_delta_f1: 0.02\n186\t  result_rationale: 'Ensemble 在 worst 档下彻底失败，原因链： (1) 三个信号 overlap 极低（pairwise Jaccard\n187\t    < 0.15）→ majority vote 几乎不触发（recall 9%）； (2) 加权融合稍好但 cross-validation 权重不稳定（std/mean\n188\t    > 0.6）——reviewer 说 \"overfitting to a small calibration set with unstable weights\n189\t    is not a methodology contribution\"； (3) Optimized vs uniform weight F1 差异仅 0.02——\"no\n190\t    evidence that learned fusion outperforms naive averaging, suggesting insufficient\n191\t    signal diversity\"； (4) DIF weight 仅 0.28（最低），ConStat 0.51——reviewer 读为 \"even the\n192\t    ensemble downweights DIF, your supposed primary contribution\"； (5) FPR=0.087 达标（<0.10），但\n193\t    recall=0.15 意味着 85% contamination 未检测—— \"an ensemble that misses 85% of contaminated\n194\t    items is not operationally useful\"。 核心问题：Claim 2（ensemble = contribution）在 worst\n195\t    档下被视为 negative result， 不是 contribution——\"showing that three weak detectors don''t\n196\t    combine well is not novel\"。\n197\t\n198\t    '\n199\t  tables:\n200\t  - 'Table: Ensemble configurations — all recall < 0.20, precision < 0.50'\n201\t  - 'Table: Cross-validation fold weights — high variance across folds'\n202\t  figures_description:\n203\t  - 'Fig: Precision-recall curves for individual signals and ensemble — ensemble barely\n204\t    improves over best individual'\n205\t  analysis: 'Ensemble 在 paper 中降级为 appendix negative result。Reviewer 的结论性评价： \"The\n206\t    ensemble experiment confirms what the low pairwise overlaps predicted — these\n207\t    methods detect different phenomena (or noise), and combining them doesn''t produce\n208\t    a coherent detector. This is informative but not a contribution; it''s a null\n209\t    result.\"\n210\t\n211\t    '\n212\t- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n213\t  plan_id: plan_004\n214\t  description: GSM8K 上复制 DIF 分析，用 GSM1K 作为 contamination ground truth\n215\t  expected_results:\n216\t    gsm8k_n_items: 1319\n217\t    gsm8k_n_ref: 1017\n218\t    gsm8k_n_foc: 804\n219\t    gsm8k_standard_c_pct: 18.9\n220\t    gsm8k_external_c_pct: 47.4\n221\t    gsm8k_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n222\t    semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n223\t    gsm1k_n_models: 33\n224\t    gsm1k_pearson_r: -0.478\n225\t    gsm1k_pearson_p: 0.005\n226\t    gsm1k_spearman_rho: -0.403\n227\t    gsm1k_bca_ci_upper: -0.155\n228\t    gsm1k_partial_r: -0.385\n229\t    reviewer_dismiss_gsm1k: true\n230\t  result_rationale: '数据与 registry 一致。Worst 档下 reviewer 的攻击矩阵： (1) N=33 模型——\"33 data\n231\t    points with r=-0.478 is suggestive at best; BCa CI upper bound |r|=0.155 means\n232\t    the true effect could be trivially small\"； (2) 负相关方向 (r=-0.478) 与 contamination\n233\t    hypothesis 相反——DIF items 上 contamination gap 更小，不是更大。Paper 解释为 \"DIF items resist\n234\t    contamination-based gains\"， reviewer 替代解读：\"DIF items are simply harder items where\n235\t    all models struggle, contaminated or not — the negative correlation is a difficulty\n236\t    confound, not a detection signal\"； (3) Spearman CI [−0.687, −0.031] 上界接近 0——\"barely\n237\t    significant, and with N=33 a single influential point shifts everything\"（尽管 Cook''s\n238\t    D robust, leave-one-out stable）； (4) GSM8K 是 single-domain math benchmark, MMLU\n239\t    是 57-subject multidomain—— \"generalization from GSM8K to MMLU is not justified;\n240\t    the DIF mechanism operates differently on unidimensional vs multidimensional benchmarks\"；\n241\t    (5) GSM1K 本身作为 ground truth 被质疑——\"GSM1K measures a different construct (novel\n242\t    math problems) and the gap may reflect test-taking strategy differences, not contamination\"。\n243\t    核心：A6 不成立——GSM1K 被 dismiss。\n244\t\n245\t    '\n246\t  tables:\n247\t  - 'Table: GSM1K correlation — r=-0.478 with wide CI, reviewer highlights N=33 limitation'\n248\t  - 'Table: Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=0.818 — reviewer acknowledges but says ''synthetic\n249\t    ≠ real'''\n250\t  figures_description:\n251\t  - 'Fig: Scatter plot N=33 models, DIF-C accuracy vs contamination gap — reviewer\n252\t    draws attention to sparse coverage and leverage points'\n253\t  analysis: 'GSM8K semi-synthetic (ΔTPR=0.818) 是最强结果，但 reviewer 将其与 MMLU 主分析隔离： \"The\n254\t    GSM8K semi-synthetic result is impressive but says nothing about whether the 31.3%\n255\t    MMLU finding is real or artifact — different benchmark, different dimensionality,\n256\t    different N.\" GSM1K correlation 被 dismiss due to N=33 和 difficulty confound alternative\n257\t    explanation。\n258\t\n259\t    '\n260\t- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n261\t  plan_id: plan_005\n262\t  description: Bifactor IRT equating pilot — general factor + subject-specific factors\n263\t  expected_results:\n264\t    bifactor_convergence: false\n265\t    rmsea: 0.089\n266\t    cfi: 0.71\n267\t    tli: 0.68\n268\t    srmr: 0.112\n269\t    n_heywood_cases: 47\n270\t    anchor_items_identified: 0\n271\t    equated_score_rho: null\n272\t    decision: killed\n273\t  result_rationale: '与 registry (plan_015 killed) 一致。Worst 档下 bifactor 失败的机制： (1)\n274\t    12,508 items × 5,227 models 的 bifactor model（general + 57 subject factors） 参数空间巨大（~12,508\n275\t    × 59 = ~738K parameters），mirt 不收敛； (2) 即使降到 subset（5 subjects, ~1,200 items），Heywood\n276\t    cases（负方差估计）出现 47 次—— 说明 data 不支持 bifactor structure，或者需要 constrained estimation；\n277\t    (3) RMSEA=0.089 > 0.06 cutoff, CFI=0.71 < 0.90 cutoff——fit 远低于 acceptable 标准；\n278\t    (4) 无法识别 anchor items（因为 model 本身不 fit）→ 整个 equating pipeline 断裂； (5) Reviewer\n279\t    的解读最致命：\"You can''t even fit a bifactor model to this data — this CONFIRMS that\n280\t    IRT assumptions are fundamentally violated for MMLU. If bifactor doesn''t fit,\n281\t    your 1D MH-DIF is even more misspecified than we thought.\" 这个 killed experiment\n282\t    在 worst 档下反而成为 reviewer 攻击 IRT misspecification 的额外弹药。\n283\t\n284\t    '\n285\t  tables:\n286\t  - 'Table: Bifactor fit indices — all below acceptable thresholds'\n287\t  figures_description:\n288\t  - 'Fig: Convergence diagnostics — oscillating log-likelihood, Heywood cases marked'\n289\t  analysis: 'Bifactor 失败在 worst 档下是 double-edged：不仅 equating 路径 dead， 还为 reviewer\n290\t    提供了 \"see, even the authors tried to fix IRT misspecification and failed\" 的叙事。\n291\t    在 reframe 路径 B（MIRT upgrade）中需要换 exploratory MIRT 或 mixture IRT 而非 confirmatory\n292\t    bifactor。\n293\t\n294\t    '\n295\t- name: item_generation_calibration\n296\t  plan_id: plan_006\n297\t  description: LLM 生成替换 items + student simulation 校准\n298\t  expected_results:\n299\t    n_items_generated: 500\n300\t    difficulty_rho_prompt_based: 0.18\n301\t    difficulty_rho_student_sim: 0.52\n302\t    target_difficulty_rho: 0.75\n303\t    construct_alignment_human_eval: 0.64\n304\t    holdout_panel_correlation: 0.41\n305\t    replacement_quality_verdict: below_benchmark\n306\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 item generation 全面低于 benchmarks： (1) Prompt-based difficulty\n307\t    targeting ρ=0.18（文献报告 0.10-0.45 range 的下端）； (2) Student simulation 校准 ρ=0.52（文献报告\n308\t    0.75-0.82 的下限以下）—— MMLU 的 domain diversity 使得单一 student simulator 无法准确估计 57 subjects\n309\t    的 difficulty； (3) Construct alignment human evaluation 仅 0.64——36% 的生成 items 被判定\n310\t    与原 item 不在同一 cognitive level 或 subject boundary 内； (4) Holdout model panel correlation\n311\t    0.41——替换 items 上的 model ranking 与原 items ranking 相关性太低，equating 无法保证 score equivalence；\n312\t    (5) Reviewer 的攻击：\"If you can''t generate calibrated replacement items, the entire\n313\t    benchmark regeneration pipeline is aspirational, not operational. This undermines\n314\t    Claim 3''s practical value.\" 依赖 plan_005 的 anchor items 识别，而 plan_005 已 killed\n315\t    → 整条 pipeline dead。\n316\t\n317\t    '\n318\t  tables:\n319\t  - 'Table: Difficulty calibration — prompt-based vs student-sim vs target, all below\n320\t    threshold'\n321\t  figures_description:\n322\t  - 'Fig: Predicted vs actual item difficulty scatter — wide dispersion, ρ=0.52'\n323\t  analysis: 'Item generation 在 worst 档下是 Claim 3（benchmark regeneration）的棺材钉。 即使不考虑\n324\t    bifactor failure，生成 items 的质量本身不足以支撑 \"operational replacement\" 的 claim。 Reviewer\n325\t    建议 \"demote to future work\"——which is exactly what the reframe paths do。\n326\t\n327\t    '\n328\t- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n329\t  plan_id: plan_007\n330\t  description: Cumulative Bayesian DIF priors — 4 successive administrations模拟\n331\t  expected_results:\n332\t    single_admin_power_d10: 0.38\n333\t    cumulative_2_admin_power_d10: 0.49\n334\t    cumulative_3_admin_power_d10: 0.58\n335\t    cumulative_4_admin_power_d10: 0.64\n336\t    target_cumulative_power: 0.7\n337\t    simulation_only: true\n338\t    real_data_validation: none\n339\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 cumulative Bayesian DIF 问题： (1) 即使 4 次 administration\n340\t    后 power 仅 0.64，低于 target 0.70—— prior accumulation 的增益被 IRT misspecification 的\n341\t    systematic bias 抵消； (2) 纯 simulation，无 real data validation——reviewer 说 \"simulation\n342\t    under your assumed generative model will always confirm your method; this is tautological\"；\n343\t    (3) \"4 successive administrations\" 假设 benchmark 不变——但如果 items 在 generation 之间\n344\t    确实 drift（即你自己的 Claim 1），则 prior 积累的是 stale information； (4) Sinharay et al. (2006)\n345\t    原始方法设计为 human testing with stable construct—— LLM benchmark 的 rapid capability\n346\t    shift 违反了 prior accumulation 的 stationarity 假设； (5) Reviewer 直接 dismiss：\"Simulation-only,\n347\t    no real data, questionable assumptions about temporal stationarity. Appendix material\n348\t    at best.\"\n349\t\n350\t    '\n351\t  tables:\n352\t  - 'Table: Power accumulation over 4 administrations — falls short of 0.70 target\n353\t    at δ=1.0'\n354\t  figures_description:\n355\t  - 'Fig: Power curves by number of accumulated administrations — reviewer annotates\n356\t    ''simulation only'' and ''stationarity violated'''\n357\t  analysis: 'Cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 worst 档下是 appendix filler，不贡献 novelty 也不贡献\n358\t    empirical evidence。 Reviewer consensus: underdeveloped simulation study without\n359\t    real-data anchoring。\n360\t\n361\t    '\n362\t- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n363\t  plan_id: plan_008\n364\t  description: Benchmark validity degradation under progressive item replacement\n365\t  expected_results:\n366\t    rho_at_5pct_replacement: 0.994\n367\t    rho_at_10pct_replacement: 0.986\n368\t    rho_at_20pct_replacement: 0.961\n369\t    rho_at_50pct_replacement: 0.873\n370\t    reliability_alpha_original: 0.94\n371\t    reliability_alpha_at_20pct: 0.88\n372\t    construct_coverage_gap_at_20pct: 3 subjects lose >30% items\n373\t    theoretical_bound_tight: false\n374\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 graceful degradation 的问题： (1) 依赖 plan_005/006 的替换 items——两者都\n375\t    failed/below benchmark， 因此 \"replacement\" 实际上是 random item removal，不是 calibrated\n376\t    replacement； (2) ρ at 20% replacement = 0.961 看似 ok，但 reviewer 用 plan_017 的结果反驳：\n377\t    \"You already showed ρ≈0.997 when removing 31% DIF items. Random replacement at\n378\t    20% gives ρ=0.961 — WORSE than just removing items entirely. Your replacement\n379\t    items ADD noise.\"； (3) Reliability alpha 从 0.94 降到 0.88——\"degradation is measurable\n380\t    and concerning at only 20% replacement\"； (4) 3 subjects lose >30% items at 20%\n381\t    replacement rate——construct coverage 不均匀， 某些 domain 被 disproportionately 影响； (5)\n382\t    Theoretical bounds 不 tight——无法给出 \"replace up to X% safely\" 的 actionable threshold，\n383\t    削弱 practical contribution。\n384\t\n385\t    '\n386\t  tables:\n387\t  - 'Table: Validity metrics × replacement rate — degradation faster than expected'\n388\t  figures_description:\n389\t  - 'Fig: ρ vs replacement rate curve — comparison with pure removal shows replacement\n390\t    adds noise'\n391\t  analysis: '在 bifactor 和 item generation 都失败的前提下，graceful degradation 变成 \"removing\n392\t    items\" 分析而非 \"replacing items\" 分析。与 plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997 冲突——removing DIF items 更安全\n393\t    than replacing them with poorly calibrated alternatives。Reviewer 结论： \"The regeneration\n394\t    pipeline is not ready for deployment.\"\n395\t\n396\t    '\n397\t- name: item_focused_trees\n398\t  plan_id: plan_009\n399\t  description: Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger 2016) — continuous temporal covariate\n400\t    DIF\n401\t  expected_results:\n402\t    ift_n_items_flagged: 4102\n403\t    ift_vs_mh_jaccard: 0.48\n404\t    ift_unique_flags: 1834\n405\t    mh_unique_flags: 1650\n406\t    ift_first_split_variable: release_date\n407\t    ift_interaction_with_size: significant (p<0.01)\n408\t    ift_temporal_granularity: quarterly splits emerge naturally\n409\t  result_rationale: 'IFT 在 worst 档下成为双刃剑： (1) IFT flags 4,102 items (32.8%) vs MH\n410\t    flags 3,918 (31.3%)——数量相近但 overlap 仅 48%， meaning 52% 的 flags 不一致； (2) Reviewer\n411\t    解读：\"Two DIF methods on the same data flag different items — this means at least\n412\t    one (probably both) is detecting noise, not signal. If the phenomenon were real\n413\t    and large, methods should converge.\"； (3) IFT 的 continuous treatment 本身挑战了 MH\n414\t    的 binary temporal split—— \"IFT shows the split is not clean at your chosen cutoff;\n415\t    DIF is gradual across the timeline, suggesting capability drift not contamination\n416\t    events\"； (4) IFT interaction with model size (p<0.01) 引入新 confound—— \"bigger models\n417\t    released later AND are more capable, so temporal DIF = size+capability confound\"；\n418\t    (5) IFT 作为 robustness check 未能 confirm MH——在 worst 档下这是 negative evidence。\n419\t\n420\t    '\n421\t  tables:\n422\t  - 'Table: MH vs IFT flag comparison — 48% Jaccard, significant disagreement'\n423\t  figures_description:\n424\t  - 'Fig: IFT tree structure — first split on date, second on model size — reviewer\n425\t    reads as confound evidence'\n426\t  analysis: 'IFT 本意是 \"alternative method validates MH\"，但 worst 档下 48% overlap 被读为\n427\t    refutation。 Reviewer 的 steel-man 攻击：\"If items'' DIF status depends on which method\n428\t    you use, the phenomenon is not robust — it''s an artifact of methodological choices.\"\n429\t    IFT 降级为 appendix，与主 finding 的 tension 在 limitations 中 discuss。\n430\t\n431\t    '\n432\t- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n433\t  plan_id: plan_010\n434\t  description: Decoder-only 子群内 DIF 分析 — 测试 architecture heterogeneity 影响\n435\t  expected_results:\n436\t    n_decoder_only: 5226\n437\t    n_non_decoder: 1\n438\t    decoder_only_c_pct: 31.3\n439\t    full_population_c_pct: 31.3\n440\t    jaccard_decoder_vs_full: 1.0\n441\t    rmsea_decoder_only: 0.087\n442\t    cfi_decoder_only: 0.73\n443\t    tlr_decoder_only: 0.7\n444\t    irt_lz_pct_above_2_decoder_only: 97.8\n445\t  result_rationale: '与 paper_framing 一致——METABENCH MMLU 是 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227)。\n446\t    Worst 档下这个实验 backfires： (1) Removing 1 non-decoder model 什么都不改变 (Jaccard=1.0,\n447\t    C% identical)—— reviewer 说 \"this is a vacuous robustness check; with 1 non-decoder\n448\t    model, architecture stratification is meaningless\"； (2) 真正的问题是 IRT fit——RMSEA=0.087,\n449\t    CFI=0.73, |Lz|>2 仍然 97.8%—— \"decoder-only homogeneity doesn''t fix IRT misspecification\n450\t    because the misfit comes from 57-subject multidimensionality, not architecture\n451\t    mixing\"； (3) Reviewer 的核心反驳：\"You showed architecture isn''t the problem — fine.\n452\t    But you still haven''t addressed THE problem: multidimensional ability with 1D\n453\t    matching. Removing 1 model is irrelevant; fitting a multidimensional IRT model\n454\t    is what''s needed.\"； (4) 实验在 paper_framing 中被列为 \"✅ RESOLVED\"，但 worst 档 reviewer\n455\t    认为 它 resolved a non-issue while ignoring the actual issue。\n456\t\n457\t    '\n458\t  tables:\n459\t  - 'Table: Full vs decoder-only DIF — identical results, confirming architecture\n460\t    is not the confound'\n461\t  figures_description:\n462\t  - 'Fig: IRT fit indices — still poor even in homogeneous subgroup'\n463\t  analysis: 'Architecture stratification 是一个 true-but-trivial result。99.98% decoder-only\n464\t    意味着 这个 check 从设计上就不可能找到 architecture effect。Reviewer 用它作为 \"authors address the\n465\t    wrong confound\" 的证据——the real confound is multidimensionality, not architecture。\n466\t    在 reframe 路径下，这个实验仍然 reportable but not defensive。\n467\t\n468\t    '\n469\t- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n470\t  plan_id: plan_011\n471\t  description: Known contamination injection into real METABENCH matrix — controlled\n472\t    ground truth\n473\t  expected_results:\n474\t    n_clean_items_selected: 500\n475\t    n_injected_items: 200\n476\t    temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n477\t    temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.548\n478\t    temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.834\n479\t    temporal_external_tpr_p10: 1.0\n480\t    temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n481\t    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n482\t    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n483\t    ability_external_tpr_p10: 0.8\n484\t    ability_external_fpr: 0.493\n485\t    standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.298→0.616\n486\t    matching_variable_contamination: true\n487\t    cross_subject_delta_fpr: 0.0\n488\t  result_rationale: '与 registry 一致。Semi-synthetic 是 paper 最强技术贡献，但 worst 档下： (1) baseline\n489\t    FPR=0.314——\"even before injection, 31.4% items are flagged. ΔTPR is measured against\n490\t    this inflated baseline, so the ''detection power'' is really ''additional flags\n491\t    on top of already-massive false positive rate''\"； (2) Reviewer 的关键攻击：ΔTPR=0.508\n492\t    at p=0.5 means \"if half the focal group memorizes an item, DIF has 50% chance\n493\t    of catching it ON TOP of 31% baseline noise. In absolute terms, you flag 83.4%\n494\t    of injected items — but you also flag 31.4% of clean items. Your precision is\n495\t    ~(0.508×200)/(0.508×200+0.314×300) ≈ 52%.\"； (3) injection mechanism (incorrect→correct\n496\t    flip) 是 simplification—— \"real contamination doesn''t flip all wrong answers to\n497\t    correct; partial memorization produces answer-distribution shifts, not binary\n498\t    flips\"； (4) FPR inflation under standard matching (0.298→0.616) 虽然被 cross-subject\n499\t    matching 解决 (ΔFPR=0.000)，但 reviewer 质疑 cross-subject matching 本身： \"using other-subject\n500\t    scores as matching variable assumes subjects are independent — but Q3 analysis\n501\t    (plan_013) showed cross-subject |Q3| can reach 0.20+\"； (5) 最深层攻击：injection into\n502\t    a matrix where 1D IRT is already misspecified → \"you''re testing detection power\n503\t    of a misspecified method on a misspecified baseline; positive ΔTPR doesn''t validate\n504\t    the method, it validates that adding signal to a noisy detector shifts its output\"。\n505\t    尽管如此，ΔTPR dose-response (0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0 : 0.548→0.834→0.99→1.0) 和 cross-subject\n506\t    ΔFPR=0.000 仍然是 technically impressive，reviewer 不否认技术执行， 而是质疑其 interpretive value\n507\t    given misspecification。\n508\t\n509\t    '\n510\t  tables:\n511\t  - 'Table: Semi-synthetic TPR/FPR across injection rates — reviewer annotates baseline\n512\t    FPR as ''the real story'''\n513\t  - 'Table: Standard vs cross-subject matching — ΔFPR=0.000 is acknowledged but Q3\n514\t    caveat raised'\n515\t  figures_description:\n516\t  - 'Fig: Dose-response curve ΔTPR vs p — clean sigmoid, but reviewer adds dotted\n517\t    line at FPR=0.314 baseline'\n518\t  - 'Fig: Cross-subject vs within-subject FPR comparison — clean result but ''independence\n519\t    assumption questionable'''\n520\t  analysis: Semi-synthetic 在 worst 档下从 \"validates DIF\" 被重新解读为 \"validates that injecting\n521\t    signal into a high-FPR detector produces more flags.\" Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000)\n522\t    是 最 defensible 的技术结果，但被 reviewer 用 Q3 cross-subject correlation 削弱。 在 reframe\n523\t    路径 A（Framework-first）中，这个实验升为 primary contribution—— 即使 reviewer 攻击 MMLU DIF 本身，framework\n524\t    的 reusability 和 ΔFPR=0.000 innovation 仍有独立价值。这是 worst 档下最有 salvage potential 的实验。\n525\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1de34d84-f766-4404-96e4-471a6ac5107f","uuid":"4a553380-4aa7-4559-b7f2-956295d8f821","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:09:14.062Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T062008/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '核心叙事：novelty 被彻底否定（\"applying textbook MH 1988 to new data ≠ contribution\"），IRT\n  misspecification 被视为 根本性方法论缺陷（\"98% |Lz|>2 → ability matching 系统性偏差 → 31% C% 是 artifact\n  而非 finding\"）， semi-synthetic framework 被认为 too simple to publish，meta-critique 被\n  dismiss 为 obvious。 每个实验的结果要么被重新解读为 artifact，要么被认为 underpowered/scope-limited。 reviewer\n  立场：3 位中 2-3 位给 reject，平均分 3.5，novelty sub-score 1.5。 三条 reframe 路径（Framework-first\n  / MIRT upgrade / Benchmark science）是唯一出路。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: METABENCH MMLU 5,227×12,508 response matrix 上的 MH-DIF 分析\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n    temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.318\n    temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n    ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n    within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n    domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n    domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n    sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n    irt_lz_pct_above_2: 98\n    reviewer_interpretation: artifact_of_misspecification\n  result_rationale: '数据本身与已完成 registry 一致——31.3% C% 是真实观测。但在 worst 档下，reviewer 的解读路径是：\n    (1) 98% 模型 |Lz|>2 表明 1D IRT ability estimates 系统性不可靠； (2) MH 的 ability matching\n    依赖 total score 作为 ability proxy，而 MMLU 57 subjects 的 multidimensionality 意味着 total\n    score 是一个 collapsed composite，无法真正 match ability； (3) 因此 31.3% C% 中有大量是 ability\n    confounding 造成的 spurious DIF—— 两个模型在不同 subject domains 上能力结构不同，但 total score 相近，被\n    MH 视为 \"matched\"， 实际上它们在特定 subject 上的 ability 并不 matched； (4) enrichment≈0.96 直接验证了\n    DIF flags 与已知 contamination labels 无关联—— reviewer 读为 \"你的方法检测不到 contamination\"；\n    (5) 0.18% sanity check 虽然证明不是纯噪声，但 reviewer 认为这只是证明 temporal cohort 之间 确实存在 ability\n    distribution shift，而非 item-level contamination。 ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 被 reviewer 解读为\n    \"domain improvement 是 confound 的证据， 不是被排除的证据\"——因为 item-level decomposition (plan_019)\n    的 pseudo R²=0.0007 只说明 linear relationship 弱，不排除 nonlinear 或 interaction effects。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1: Temporal DIF results — C%=31.3%, enrichment=0.96 — reviewer 标注 ''enrichment≈1\n    = no detection value'''\n  - 'Table 2: Cohort comparison — ability split C%=2.9% vs temporal 31.3% — reviewer\n    认为差异来自 ability shift 而非 item-level effect'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: DIF effect size distribution — reviewer 指出 continuous distribution without\n    bimodality suggests no distinct ''contaminated'' subpopulation, consistent with\n    model misfit gradual shift'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 的核心攻击：31.3% 是一个 misspecified model 下的 baseline rate，不是 finding。\n    类比：如果你用线性回归拟合非线性数据，residual patterns 不代表新发现，而代表 model misfit。 MH-DIF on multidimensional\n    data with 1D matching = structural Type I error inflation。 Llama-2 vs Llama-3\n    within-family C%=61.3% 被读为更强的证据——\"同一 family 内 61% items show DIF = 显然是 ability\n    structure change, not contamination\"。\n\n    '\n- name: rl_robustness_validation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 验证 DIF 对 reasoning-RL 模型（GRPO/PPO）的鲁棒性\n  expected_results:\n    n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n    alignment_rl_cohort_n: 477\n    grpo_cohort_dif_c_pct: 34.8\n    sft_baseline_dif_c_pct: 30.2\n    alignment_rl_dif_c_pct: 31.9\n    jaccard_sft_vs_grpo: 0.71\n    delong_p_dif_vs_constat: 0.38\n    tost_equivalence_p: 0.22\n    constat_auroc_on_rl: 0.54\n    mink_auroc_on_rl: 0.51\n    dif_auroc_on_rl: 0.58\n    bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif:\n    - 0.41\n    - 0.73\n    power_at_p04: 0.12\n    power_at_p07: 0.43\n    power_at_p10: 0.68\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下的问题不是实验跑不出来，而是 N=13 reasoning-RL 模型被 reviewer 视为 fundamentally\n    underpowered： (1) 13 个 GRPO/PPO 模型混入 focal cohort 后，C% 从 30.2% 微升到 34.8%—— reviewer\n    解读为 \"adding stronger models → more ability confounding → more spurious DIF\"， 而非\n    \"DIF robust to RL\"； (2) AUROC 比较（DIF 0.58 vs ConStat 0.54 vs Min-K% 0.51）差异不显著（DeLong\n    p=0.38）， bootstrap CI 跨越 0.5——reviewer 说 \"all methods are at chance, you''ve shown\n    nothing\"； (3) TOST equivalence test p=0.22，无法 reject \"DIF 和传统方法等效\" 的 H0—— reviewer\n    认为 \"failure to demonstrate equivalence or superiority = uninformative\"； (4) Power\n    analysis 显示 p=0.4 时 TPR=0.12——reviewer 说 \"DIF can only detect near-complete exploitation,\n    which is the trivial case\"； (5) 核心问题：整个实验无法区分 \"DIF works on RL models\" 和 \"DIF\n    produces same artifacts regardless of model type\"——在 IRT misspecification 框架下，两者不可区分。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: AUROC comparison across 3 methods × 3 cohort types — all CIs overlap,\n    no method dominates'\n  - 'Table: Power curve p ∈ [0.4, 1.0] — reviewer notes ''useful range starts at p≥0.7,\n    narrowing practical applicability'''\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Bootstrap AUROC distributions — heavy overlap among DIF/ConStat/Min-K%,\n    all centered near 0.55'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer consensus: \"N=13 RL models is a pilot, not a validation. The\n    authors cannot claim RL-robustness based on mixing 13 models into a 600+ cohort\n    — the signal is drowned. Individual-model analysis (ConStat/Min-K%) at least tests\n    each model; DIF by design cannot. This is a structural limitation of group-level\n    methods, acknowledged but not resolved.\" 致命打击：reviewer 将此解读为 DIF 的固有缺陷——无法做 per-model\n    detection——而非优势。\n\n    '\n- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003a\n  description: ConStat-style perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的独立评估\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_reformulated: 220\n    reformulation_quality_human_eval: 0.82\n    constat_detection_rate_non_rl: 0.41\n    constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.08\n    constat_fdr_controlled_rate: 0.23\n    constat_vs_dif_overlap_pct: 12.7\n    constat_fpr: 0.067\n    constat_unique_detections: 158\n    dif_unique_detections: 892\n  result_rationale: 'ConStat 在 non-RL 模型上表现合理（41% detection rate），FPR 远低于 DIF（0.067\n    vs 0.318）。 Worst 档下 reviewer 解读： (1) ConStat FPR=0.067 vs DIF FPR=0.318——\"DIF\n    的高 detection rate 主要来自高 FPR， 不是真正的 detection power\"； (2) 12.7% overlap 表明两种方法检测的是完全不同的现象——reviewer\n    认为 ConStat 检测 actual contamination (perturbation sensitivity)，而 DIF 检测 ability\n    shift artifact； (3) ConStat 在 RL 模型上确实退化（8%），但 reviewer 说 \"at least ConStat has\n    a clear mechanism story; DIF''s mechanism is unfalsifiable because any result\n    can be attributed to either contamination or ability change\"； (4) 220 items 的\n    reformulation 质量（0.82 human eval）足够，但 scope 太小—— reviewer 要求 full-scale replication\n    才能比较。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: ConStat vs DIF detection comparison — ConStat lower recall but much lower\n    FPR'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Venn diagram of ConStat vs DIF detections — minimal overlap underscores\n    different phenomena detected'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 用 ConStat 的低 FPR 作为武器：\"ConStat achieves controlled FPR by design\n    (FDR correction); DIF''s 31.8% FPR on Li-clean items means nearly 1 in 3 flags\n    is false, and you cannot tell which ones without ground truth.\" 这强化了 \"DIF C% is\n    inflated by misspecification\" 的叙事。\n\n    '\n- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的独立评估\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_evaluated: 12\n    n_items_per_model: 200\n    n_generations_per_item: 50\n    bimodal_detection_rate: 0.14\n    variance_based_detection_rate: 0.22\n    dvd_vs_dif_overlap: 0.09\n    dvd_fpr: 0.04\n    gpu_hours_used: 65\n    variant_contamination_detected: 31\n  result_rationale: 'DVD 需要 per-model inference access（50 generations × 200 items\n    × 12 models = 120K generations）， cost 高但可行。Worst 档下： (1) Bimodal detection rate\n    仅 14%——reviewer 说 \"variant contamination is rare or this method is underpowered,\n    either way not compelling\"； (2) 9% overlap with DIF——再次证明方法检测不同现象，但 worst 档下 reviewer\n    解读为 \"three orthogonal weak signals don''t add up to one strong signal\"； (3) DVD\n    FPR=0.04 很低，但 detection rate 也低——reviewer 认为 precision-recall tradeoff 不足以支撑 contribution；\n    (4) 12 models 太少——reviewer 要求 \"at minimum 50+ models to characterize generation\n    variance distribution\"，而 GPU budget 不支持。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: DVD detection rates by contamination type (verbatim vs variant) — low\n    overall'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Generation variance histograms per model — most items unimodal, bimodal\n    signal weak'\n  analysis: 'DVD 作为独立信号太弱（14% bimodal detection），且 per-model inference 的 cost 使其不\n    scalable。 Reviewer 建议 \"DVD is better suited as a follow-up diagnostic on flagged\n    items, not a primary detector\" ——削弱 ensemble 的 motivation。\n\n    '\n- name: ensemble_fusion\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合\n  expected_results:\n    majority_vote_precision: 0.38\n    majority_vote_recall: 0.09\n    weighted_fusion_precision: 0.44\n    weighted_fusion_recall: 0.15\n    ensemble_fpr: 0.087\n    cross_val_weight_stability: low — std/mean > 0.6 across folds\n    dif_weight: 0.28\n    constat_weight: 0.51\n    dvd_weight: 0.21\n    uniform_baseline_vs_optimized_delta_f1: 0.02\n  result_rationale: 'Ensemble 在 worst 档下彻底失败，原因链： (1) 三个信号 overlap 极低（pairwise Jaccard\n    < 0.15）→ majority vote 几乎不触发（recall 9%）； (2) 加权融合稍好但 cross-validation 权重不稳定（std/mean\n    > 0.6）——reviewer 说 \"overfitting to a small calibration set with unstable weights\n    is not a methodology contribution\"； (3) Optimized vs uniform weight F1 差异仅 0.02——\"no\n    evidence that learned fusion outperforms naive averaging, suggesting insufficient\n    signal diversity\"； (4) DIF weight 仅 0.28（最低），ConStat 0.51——reviewer 读为 \"even the\n    ensemble downweights DIF, your supposed primary contribution\"； (5) FPR=0.087 达标（<0.10），但\n    recall=0.15 意味着 85% contamination 未检测—— \"an ensemble that misses 85% of contaminated\n    items is not operationally useful\"。 核心问题：Claim 2（ensemble = contribution）在 worst\n    档下被视为 negative result， 不是 contribution——\"showing that three weak detectors don''t\n    combine well is not novel\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Ensemble configurations — all recall < 0.20, precision < 0.50'\n  - 'Table: Cross-validation fold weights — high variance across folds'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Precision-recall curves for individual signals and ensemble — ensemble barely\n    improves over best individual'\n  analysis: 'Ensemble 在 paper 中降级为 appendix negative result。Reviewer 的结论性评价： \"The\n    ensemble experiment confirms what the low pairwise overlaps predicted — these\n    methods detect different phenomena (or noise), and combining them doesn''t produce\n    a coherent detector. This is informative but not a contribution; it''s a null\n    result.\"\n\n    '\n- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: GSM8K 上复制 DIF 分析，用 GSM1K 作为 contamination ground truth\n  expected_results:\n    gsm8k_n_items: 1319\n    gsm8k_n_ref: 1017\n    gsm8k_n_foc: 804\n    gsm8k_standard_c_pct: 18.9\n    gsm8k_external_c_pct: 47.4\n    gsm8k_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n    semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n    gsm1k_n_models: 33\n    gsm1k_pearson_r: -0.478\n    gsm1k_pearson_p: 0.005\n    gsm1k_spearman_rho: -0.403\n    gsm1k_bca_ci_upper: -0.155\n    gsm1k_partial_r: -0.385\n    reviewer_dismiss_gsm1k: true\n  result_rationale: '数据与 registry 一致。Worst 档下 reviewer 的攻击矩阵： (1) N=33 模型——\"33 data\n    points with r=-0.478 is suggestive at best; BCa CI upper bound |r|=0.155 means\n    the true effect could be trivially small\"； (2) 负相关方向 (r=-0.478) 与 contamination\n    hypothesis 相反——DIF items 上 contamination gap 更小，不是更大。Paper 解释为 \"DIF items resist\n    contamination-based gains\"， reviewer 替代解读：\"DIF items are simply harder items where\n    all models struggle, contaminated or not — the negative correlation is a difficulty\n    confound, not a detection signal\"； (3) Spearman CI [−0.687, −0.031] 上界接近 0——\"barely\n    significant, and with N=33 a single influential point shifts everything\"（尽管 Cook''s\n    D robust, leave-one-out stable）； (4) GSM8K 是 single-domain math benchmark, MMLU\n    是 57-subject multidomain—— \"generalization from GSM8K to MMLU is not justified;\n    the DIF mechanism operates differently on unidimensional vs multidimensional benchmarks\"；\n    (5) GSM1K 本身作为 ground truth 被质疑——\"GSM1K measures a different construct (novel\n    math problems) and the gap may reflect test-taking strategy differences, not contamination\"。\n    核心：A6 不成立——GSM1K 被 dismiss。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: GSM1K correlation — r=-0.478 with wide CI, reviewer highlights N=33 limitation'\n  - 'Table: Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=0.818 — reviewer acknowledges but says ''synthetic\n    ≠ real'''\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Scatter plot N=33 models, DIF-C accuracy vs contamination gap — reviewer\n    draws attention to sparse coverage and leverage points'\n  analysis: 'GSM8K semi-synthetic (ΔTPR=0.818) 是最强结果，但 reviewer 将其与 MMLU 主分析隔离： \"The\n    GSM8K semi-synthetic result is impressive but says nothing about whether the 31.3%\n    MMLU finding is real or artifact — different benchmark, different dimensionality,\n    different N.\" GSM1K correlation 被 dismiss due to N=33 和 difficulty confound alternative\n    explanation。\n\n    '\n- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: Bifactor IRT equating pilot — general factor + subject-specific factors\n  expected_results:\n    bifactor_convergence: false\n    rmsea: 0.089\n    cfi: 0.71\n    tli: 0.68\n    srmr: 0.112\n    n_heywood_cases: 47\n    anchor_items_identified: 0\n    equated_score_rho: null\n    decision: killed\n  result_rationale: '与 registry (plan_015 killed) 一致。Worst 档下 bifactor 失败的机制： (1)\n    12,508 items × 5,227 models 的 bifactor model（general + 57 subject factors） 参数空间巨大（~12,508\n    × 59 = ~738K parameters），mirt 不收敛； (2) 即使降到 subset（5 subjects, ~1,200 items），Heywood\n    cases（负方差估计）出现 47 次—— 说明 data 不支持 bifactor structure，或者需要 constrained estimation；\n    (3) RMSEA=0.089 > 0.06 cutoff, CFI=0.71 < 0.90 cutoff——fit 远低于 acceptable 标准；\n    (4) 无法识别 anchor items（因为 model 本身不 fit）→ 整个 equating pipeline 断裂； (5) Reviewer\n    的解读最致命：\"You can''t even fit a bifactor model to this data — this CONFIRMS that\n    IRT assumptions are fundamentally violated for MMLU. If bifactor doesn''t fit,\n    your 1D MH-DIF is even more misspecified than we thought.\" 这个 killed experiment\n    在 worst 档下反而成为 reviewer 攻击 IRT misspecification 的额外弹药。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Bifactor fit indices — all below acceptable thresholds'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Convergence diagnostics — oscillating log-likelihood, Heywood cases marked'\n  analysis: 'Bifactor 失败在 worst 档下是 double-edged：不仅 equating 路径 dead， 还为 reviewer\n    提供了 \"see, even the authors tried to fix IRT misspecification and failed\" 的叙事。\n    在 reframe 路径 B（MIRT upgrade）中需要换 exploratory MIRT 或 mixture IRT 而非 confirmatory\n    bifactor。\n\n    '\n- name: item_generation_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: LLM 生成替换 items + student simulation 校准\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_generated: 500\n    difficulty_rho_prompt_based: 0.18\n    difficulty_rho_student_sim: 0.52\n    target_difficulty_rho: 0.75\n    construct_alignment_human_eval: 0.64\n    holdout_panel_correlation: 0.41\n    replacement_quality_verdict: below_benchmark\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 item generation 全面低于 benchmarks： (1) Prompt-based difficulty\n    targeting ρ=0.18（文献报告 0.10-0.45 range 的下端）； (2) Student simulation 校准 ρ=0.52（文献报告\n    0.75-0.82 的下限以下）—— MMLU 的 domain diversity 使得单一 student simulator 无法准确估计 57 subjects\n    的 difficulty； (3) Construct alignment human evaluation 仅 0.64——36% 的生成 items 被判定\n    与原 item 不在同一 cognitive level 或 subject boundary 内； (4) Holdout model panel correlation\n    0.41——替换 items 上的 model ranking 与原 items ranking 相关性太低，equating 无法保证 score equivalence；\n    (5) Reviewer 的攻击：\"If you can''t generate calibrated replacement items, the entire\n    benchmark regeneration pipeline is aspirational, not operational. This undermines\n    Claim 3''s practical value.\" 依赖 plan_005 的 anchor items 识别，而 plan_005 已 killed\n    → 整条 pipeline dead。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Difficulty calibration — prompt-based vs student-sim vs target, all below\n    threshold'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Predicted vs actual item difficulty scatter — wide dispersion, ρ=0.52'\n  analysis: 'Item generation 在 worst 档下是 Claim 3（benchmark regeneration）的棺材钉。 即使不考虑\n    bifactor failure，生成 items 的质量本身不足以支撑 \"operational replacement\" 的 claim。 Reviewer\n    建议 \"demote to future work\"——which is exactly what the reframe paths do。\n\n    '\n- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: Cumulative Bayesian DIF priors — 4 successive administrations模拟\n  expected_results:\n    single_admin_power_d10: 0.38\n    cumulative_2_admin_power_d10: 0.49\n    cumulative_3_admin_power_d10: 0.58\n    cumulative_4_admin_power_d10: 0.64\n    target_cumulative_power: 0.7\n    simulation_only: true\n    real_data_validation: none\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 cumulative Bayesian DIF 问题： (1) 即使 4 次 administration\n    后 power 仅 0.64，低于 target 0.70—— prior accumulation 的增益被 IRT misspecification 的\n    systematic bias 抵消； (2) 纯 simulation，无 real data validation——reviewer 说 \"simulation\n    under your assumed generative model will always confirm your method; this is tautological\"；\n    (3) \"4 successive administrations\" 假设 benchmark 不变——但如果 items 在 generation 之间\n    确实 drift（即你自己的 Claim 1），则 prior 积累的是 stale information； (4) Sinharay et al. (2006)\n    原始方法设计为 human testing with stable construct—— LLM benchmark 的 rapid capability\n    shift 违反了 prior accumulation 的 stationarity 假设； (5) Reviewer 直接 dismiss：\"Simulation-only,\n    no real data, questionable assumptions about temporal stationarity. Appendix material\n    at best.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Power accumulation over 4 administrations — falls short of 0.70 target\n    at δ=1.0'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Power curves by number of accumulated administrations — reviewer annotates\n    ''simulation only'' and ''stationarity violated'''\n  analysis: 'Cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 worst 档下是 appendix filler，不贡献 novelty 也不贡献\n    empirical evidence。 Reviewer consensus: underdeveloped simulation study without\n    real-data anchoring。\n\n    '\n- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Benchmark validity degradation under progressive item replacement\n  expected_results:\n    rho_at_5pct_replacement: 0.994\n    rho_at_10pct_replacement: 0.986\n    rho_at_20pct_replacement: 0.961\n    rho_at_50pct_replacement: 0.873\n    reliability_alpha_original: 0.94\n    reliability_alpha_at_20pct: 0.88\n    construct_coverage_gap_at_20pct: 3 subjects lose >30% items\n    theoretical_bound_tight: false\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 graceful degradation 的问题： (1) 依赖 plan_005/006 的替换 items——两者都\n    failed/below benchmark， 因此 \"replacement\" 实际上是 random item removal，不是 calibrated\n    replacement； (2) ρ at 20% replacement = 0.961 看似 ok，但 reviewer 用 plan_017 的结果反驳：\n    \"You already showed ρ≈0.997 when removing 31% DIF items. Random replacement at\n    20% gives ρ=0.961 — WORSE than just removing items entirely. Your replacement\n    items ADD noise.\"； (3) Reliability alpha 从 0.94 降到 0.88——\"degradation is measurable\n    and concerning at only 20% replacement\"； (4) 3 subjects lose >30% items at 20%\n    replacement rate——construct coverage 不均匀， 某些 domain 被 disproportionately 影响； (5)\n    Theoretical bounds 不 tight——无法给出 \"replace up to X% safely\" 的 actionable threshold，\n    削弱 practical contribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Validity metrics × replacement rate — degradation faster than expected'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: ρ vs replacement rate curve — comparison with pure removal shows replacement\n    adds noise'\n  analysis: '在 bifactor 和 item generation 都失败的前提下，graceful degradation 变成 \"removing\n    items\" 分析而非 \"replacing items\" 分析。与 plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997 冲突——removing DIF items 更安全\n    than replacing them with poorly calibrated alternatives。Reviewer 结论： \"The regeneration\n    pipeline is not ready for deployment.\"\n\n    '\n- name: item_focused_trees\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger 2016) — continuous temporal covariate\n    DIF\n  expected_results:\n    ift_n_items_flagged: 4102\n    ift_vs_mh_jaccard: 0.48\n    ift_unique_flags: 1834\n    mh_unique_flags: 1650\n    ift_first_split_variable: release_date\n    ift_interaction_with_size: significant (p<0.01)\n    ift_temporal_granularity: quarterly splits emerge naturally\n  result_rationale: 'IFT 在 worst 档下成为双刃剑： (1) IFT flags 4,102 items (32.8%) vs MH\n    flags 3,918 (31.3%)——数量相近但 overlap 仅 48%， meaning 52% 的 flags 不一致； (2) Reviewer\n    解读：\"Two DIF methods on the same data flag different items — this means at least\n    one (probably both) is detecting noise, not signal. If the phenomenon were real\n    and large, methods should converge.\"； (3) IFT 的 continuous treatment 本身挑战了 MH\n    的 binary temporal split—— \"IFT shows the split is not clean at your chosen cutoff;\n    DIF is gradual across the timeline, suggesting capability drift not contamination\n    events\"； (4) IFT interaction with model size (p<0.01) 引入新 confound—— \"bigger models\n    released later AND are more capable, so temporal DIF = size+capability confound\"；\n    (5) IFT 作为 robustness check 未能 confirm MH——在 worst 档下这是 negative evidence。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: MH vs IFT flag comparison — 48% Jaccard, significant disagreement'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: IFT tree structure — first split on date, second on model size — reviewer\n    reads as confound evidence'\n  analysis: 'IFT 本意是 \"alternative method validates MH\"，但 worst 档下 48% overlap 被读为\n    refutation。 Reviewer 的 steel-man 攻击：\"If items'' DIF status depends on which method\n    you use, the phenomenon is not robust — it''s an artifact of methodological choices.\"\n    IFT 降级为 appendix，与主 finding 的 tension 在 limitations 中 discuss。\n\n    '\n- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Decoder-only 子群内 DIF 分析 — 测试 architecture heterogeneity 影响\n  expected_results:\n    n_decoder_only: 5226\n    n_non_decoder: 1\n    decoder_only_c_pct: 31.3\n    full_population_c_pct: 31.3\n    jaccard_decoder_vs_full: 1.0\n    rmsea_decoder_only: 0.087\n    cfi_decoder_only: 0.73\n    tlr_decoder_only: 0.7\n    irt_lz_pct_above_2_decoder_only: 97.8\n  result_rationale: '与 paper_framing 一致——METABENCH MMLU 是 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227)。\n    Worst 档下这个实验 backfires： (1) Removing 1 non-decoder model 什么都不改变 (Jaccard=1.0,\n    C% identical)—— reviewer 说 \"this is a vacuous robustness check; with 1 non-decoder\n    model, architecture stratification is meaningless\"； (2) 真正的问题是 IRT fit——RMSEA=0.087,\n    CFI=0.73, |Lz|>2 仍然 97.8%—— \"decoder-only homogeneity doesn''t fix IRT misspecification\n    because the misfit comes from 57-subject multidimensionality, not architecture\n    mixing\"； (3) Reviewer 的核心反驳：\"You showed architecture isn''t the problem — fine.\n    But you still haven''t addressed THE problem: multidimensional ability with 1D\n    matching. Removing 1 model is irrelevant; fitting a multidimensional IRT model\n    is what''s needed.\"； (4) 实验在 paper_framing 中被列为 \"✅ RESOLVED\"，但 worst 档 reviewer\n    认为 它 resolved a non-issue while ignoring the actual issue。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Full vs decoder-only DIF — identical results, confirming architecture\n    is not the confound'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: IRT fit indices — still poor even in homogeneous subgroup'\n  analysis: 'Architecture stratification 是一个 true-but-trivial result。99.98% decoder-only\n    意味着 这个 check 从设计上就不可能找到 architecture effect。Reviewer 用它作为 \"authors address the\n    wrong confound\" 的证据——the real confound is multidimensionality, not architecture。\n    在 reframe 路径下，这个实验仍然 reportable but not defensive。\n\n    '\n- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: Known contamination injection into real METABENCH matrix — controlled\n    ground truth\n  expected_results:\n    n_clean_items_selected: 500\n    n_injected_items: 200\n    temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n    temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.548\n    temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.834\n    temporal_external_tpr_p10: 1.0\n    temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n    ability_external_tpr_p10: 0.8\n    ability_external_fpr: 0.493\n    standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.298→0.616\n    matching_variable_contamination: true\n    cross_subject_delta_fpr: 0.0\n  result_rationale: '与 registry 一致。Semi-synthetic 是 paper 最强技术贡献，但 worst 档下： (1) baseline\n    FPR=0.314——\"even before injection, 31.4% items are flagged. ΔTPR is measured against\n    this inflated baseline, so the ''detection power'' is really ''additional flags\n    on top of already-massive false positive rate''\"； (2) Reviewer 的关键攻击：ΔTPR=0.508\n    at p=0.5 means \"if half the focal group memorizes an item, DIF has 50% chance\n    of catching it ON TOP of 31% baseline noise. In absolute terms, you flag 83.4%\n    of injected items — but you also flag 31.4% of clean items. Your precision is\n    ~(0.508×200)/(0.508×200+0.314×300) ≈ 52%.\"； (3) injection mechanism (incorrect→correct\n    flip) 是 simplification—— \"real contamination doesn''t flip all wrong answers to\n    correct; partial memorization produces answer-distribution shifts, not binary\n    flips\"； (4) FPR inflation under standard matching (0.298→0.616) 虽然被 cross-subject\n    matching 解决 (ΔFPR=0.000)，但 reviewer 质疑 cross-subject matching 本身： \"using other-subject\n    scores as matching variable assumes subjects are independent — but Q3 analysis\n    (plan_013) showed cross-subject |Q3| can reach 0.20+\"； (5) 最深层攻击：injection into\n    a matrix where 1D IRT is already misspecified → \"you''re testing detection power\n    of a misspecified method on a misspecified baseline; positive ΔTPR doesn''t validate\n    the method, it validates that adding signal to a noisy detector shifts its output\"。\n    尽管如此，ΔTPR dose-response (0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0 : 0.548→0.834→0.99→1.0) 和 cross-subject\n    ΔFPR=0.000 仍然是 technically impressive，reviewer 不否认技术执行， 而是质疑其 interpretive value\n    given misspecification。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table: Semi-synthetic TPR/FPR across injection rates — reviewer annotates baseline\n    FPR as ''the real story'''\n  - 'Table: Standard vs cross-subject matching — ΔFPR=0.000 is acknowledged but Q3\n    caveat raised'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Dose-response curve ΔTPR vs p — clean sigmoid, but reviewer adds dotted\n    line at FPR=0.314 baseline'\n  - 'Fig: Cross-subject vs within-subject FPR comparison — clean result but ''independence\n    assumption questionable'''\n  analysis: Semi-synthetic 在 worst 档下从 \"validates DIF\" 被重新解读为 \"validates that injecting\n    signal into a high-FPR detector produces more flags.\" Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000)\n    是 最 defensible 的技术结果，但被 reviewer 用 Q3 cross-subject correlation 削弱。 在 reframe\n    路径 A（Framework-first）中，这个实验升为 primary contribution—— 即使 reviewer 攻击 MMLU DIF 本身，framework\n    的 reusability 和 ΔFPR=0.000 innovation 仍有独立价值。这是 worst 档下最有 salvage potential 的实验。\n","numLines":525,"startLine":1,"totalLines":525}}}
